  {
    "insert": "Your exposé proposes research regarding the human-centered factors of medical treatments and how we need to build AI and other algorithms to make sure that these are not lost. For this, it focuses on identifying the most critical socio-emotional factors and building actionable advice from them.\n\nOverall, the exposé follows the required structure. However, there are some parts that could be improved.\n\nThe hook and following anchor and teaser should quickly catch the readers interest and then move on to explain the concrete problem and what your research aims to address or introduce. In particular, the hook and anchor together should only be a few distilled sentences. After that, the teaser should quickly introduce a rough outline of your work.\nYour current motivation takes too long to introduce your own work and ideas. It dwells a lot on the general growth and challenges of new AI models, as well as the current state of AI. It might be worth rewriting some of these parts and even removing some repetition (\"unprecedented growth,\" \"groundbreaking promises,\" \"widespread application amongst the general population,\" \"its usage continues to expand rapidly\").\nIntroducing the challenge for medical treatment earlier, and teasing that your work aims to find out how to address it, might increase the reader's motivation.\n\nFollowing the motivation, your explanation of the SOTA and the theoretical framework are well done, although they are a bit intertwined (which might not be a bad thing). However, the theoretical introduction of some frameworks is missing. Your methodology includes the use of SPSS, which could be briefly mentioned in the theoretical framework. It might also be worth expanding the explanation of TAM a bit, so that readers unfamiliar with how it works can roughly understand it. \n\nThe methodology should then follow on from these parts, explaining exactly how you plan to answer the RQs. To do this, it should introduce the studies that your work aims to conduct, as well as considerations regarding the target audience and other limitations. While your current methodology answers all of the research questions, it is still rather shallow. For example, you mention that you intend to complement the TAM with other \"socio-emotional frameworks\". These should be explained in more detail, or at least there should be a rough explanation of what these frameworks are. The study also lacks more details about the size of the target audience, how the questions for the interview are chosen, and technical details like which AI models you want to analyze. It might be worthwhile to look at more examples of the methodology and learn how to add more details here. \n\nThese are the main critiques, and there are only a few minor points left. As already mentioned, your motivation as a whole is somewhat repetitive. While the sentence structure is mostly very good, the use of colons irritates the reading flow (\"[...] by improving both: efficiency and accuracy\" and \"[...] relying on elements such as: mutual understanding, [...]\"). Removing these would help reduce the disruption of the flow. Your research questions also lack structure. Numbering them might help. It is also not entirely clear whether you intend the three questions to be sub-RQs or not, since their headings are your subtitles and only the bullet points are specific questions. Finally, you present ChatGPT as a GAI model, which it is not (it is the chat interface to the GPT model). "
  }
]